on reform to America  and national school choice week is  really a marketing tool whereby they can  raise awareness and shine a spotlight on  all the wonderful work that they do one  of the the characteristics of the  movement is that all these groups  they've been working largely  independently and they all have a  different focus some may focus on  charter schools some may focus on vouch  some may focus on anti-union so it's  been hard for them to really coordinate  and organize to work together but really  the end goal is not the same for all of  us which is to bring excellent education  to all children in America I think I'd  like to play a little video actually we  had our so we had our first national  school choice week which was in January  and we kicked off at the reason DC  offices and when all across the country  and you're going to see some of the  events and some of the media attention  and just will play the video  from january twenty third through  january 29 2011 more than 200  organizations came together for a week  of action to shine a spotlight on  effective education options for all  children first-ever national school  choice week national school choice week  this is national school choice week this  is school choice week school choice week  during the week over 150 events  celebrating school choice were held  across the nation from Sacramento to  cincinnati orlando to oregon and as far  away as Alaska and Hawaii people  celebrated the week in their own ways  oftentimes using an abundance of  creativity rallies to state capitals  town hall meetings movie screenings book  club meetings concerts beach parties  online events barbecues expose pub  nights even grandma's for charter  schools coffee houses tens of thousands  of advocates parents and concerned  citizens participated and thousands  began following national school choice  week on facebook twitter and linkedin  thought leaders from across a broad  social and political spectrum added  their 