oice week  was even brought to the floor of the US  House of Representatives I rise today in  honor of a grassroots movement is  currently taking place all across our  great nation the celebration of national  school choice week three award-winning  documentaries the cartel waiting for  superman and the lottery played a  significant role in the success of the  week over 50 screenings of the  documentaries took place across the  country Bob Bowden director of the film  The Cartel attended many of these events  himself as part of an expansive speaking  tour the education revolution tour  visited 11 major cities and held  townhall meetings with panel discussions  by well-known talk radio hosts community  leaders and education reform activists  the events drew thousands of attendees  and gained widespread national media  attention when Lisa said that this  session would be called the tipping  point for school choice I was really  excited because that's that's what  national school choice week is all about  it's an event-driven movement to raise  awareness and from the ground up I I  feel like as a sub  and soccer mom myself before I was  working at the foundation I had never  heard of school choice I thought my  school was fabulous you know I pay a lot  of money in taxes and I might house was  pretty expensive i think my school has  to be you know awesome so I think we  have a difficult job because the people  that will benefit first and most from  school choice really have the least  political the smallest political voice  it's the pits the people like me who are  voting and involved and you know  educated and living in the suburbs that  are not really bringing pressure to bear  on legislators to make changes in  education so that is job number one for  us it's really to to reach my  demographic and bring us closer to the  tipping point and you know create the  social epidemic that will make this  happen okay I'm going to ask you to one  file story ok so the would be right the  beloved movie has a little controversy  of its own where I think claire has  coined it would be gate and it happened  in Idaho and I and this just happened  last week right so I thought that it  might just see how the yellow scarves  are causing trouble around the United  States the lobbies so already the the  union's fear this scarf you should wear  it with pride you should because this  little three dollar scoff last week in  Idaho on the penultimate day of their  session they were voting on a charter  bill to lift the cap from six a year  they were trying to remove this cap so  they went out for lunch and during lunch  one of the Idaho school choice groups  they're handed out the would be to the  legislators and when they came back into  the session they were wearing these so  and you have to obtain permission to  distribute anything so correct  permission  been obtained however that information  had not made it to the floor in time  mysteriously so the the floor the  Minority Leader the Democrat stood up  and was outraged that there were  promotional gifts and these scarves were  on the floor and they were swaying the  vote and that was that was against the  house rules and he managed to table the  bill and there was only one day  remaining in the session so the bill was  tabled we got a google alert about this  while we were at a meeting and I just  couldn't even believe it I'm like oh the  whoopie has killed the charter school  bill so the next day on the last day of  the session they reintroduce a new bill  which did passed the first stage but  they didn't have time to put it through  so essentially I you know the message  here is that the unions have been paying  their politicians way too much they  could just get their vote with a  three-dollar scarf so  pretty powerful piece of fleece right  here
 

